h; \"Eiffel\"", "source": "web", "dense": 0.775, "bm25": 7.28, "dense_rank": 3, "bm25_rank": 15, "rrf": 0.02921, "selected": false}, {"text": "Excluding transmitters, the Eiffel Tower is the second tallest free-standing structure in France after the Millau Viaduct. The tower has three levels for visito", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.722, "bm25": 7.41, "dense_rank": 6, "bm25_rank": 13, "rrf": 0.02885, "selected": false}, {"text": "It was designated a monument historique in 1964, and was named part of a UNESCO World Heritage Site (\"Paris, Banks of the Seine\") in 1991. The tower is 330 metr", "source": "wikipedia", "dense": 0.652, "bm25": 7.45, "dense_rank": 11, "bm25_rank": 11, "rrf": 0.02817, "selected": false}], "selected": 3, "echo_filtered": 0, "kept": 3}, "t": 8.036}
