{"status": "claim_result", "index": 1, "result": {"claim": "The Eiffel Tower was designed by Gustave Eiffel's company.", "evidence": "Evidence 1: An engineer by training, Eiffel founded and developed a company specializing in metal structural work, whose crowning achievement was the Eiffel Tower. He devoted the last thirty years of his life to his experimental research. He is best known for the Eiffel Tower, designed by his company and built for the 1889 Universal Exposition in Paris, and his contribution to building the Statue of Liberty (Liberty Enlightening the World) in New York. Nov 9, 2025 \u00b7 Because the structure carries his name, Gustave Eiffel is often credited as sole designer. He did acquire the patent rights and led the project to completion, but primary design credit belongs to Koechlin, Nouguier, and Sauvestre\u2014the team behind the form we know. Selected from among 107 projects, it was that of Gustave Eiffel, an entrepreneur, Maurice Koechlin and Emile Nouguier, both engineers, and Stephen Sauvestre, an architect, that was accepted. Oct 2, 2026 \u00b7 Eiffel Tower, wrought-iron structure in Paris that is among the most famous landmarks in the world. It is also a technological masterpiece in building-construction history. It was designed and built (1887\u201389) by Gustave Eiffel and named in his honor. Oct 2, 2026 \u00b7 In 1867 Eiffel established his own company and, as part of his initial projects, designed the lofty, arched Gallery of Machines for the Paris Exhibition of 1867.\n\nEvidence 2: The Eiffel Tower (/ \u02c8a\u026af\u0259l / \u24d8 EYE-f\u0259l; French: Tour Eiffel [tu\u0281 \u025bf\u025bl] \u24d8) is a lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower from 1887 to 1889.\n\nEvidence 3: Eiffel was selected because of his experience with wind stresses. Eiffel devised a structure consisting of a four legged pylon to support the copper sheeting 