{"status": "claim_result", "index": 2, "result": {"claim": "The Eiffel Tower was built by Gustave Eiffel's company.", "evidence": "Evidence 1: Alexandre Gustave Eiffel (  EYE-f\u0259l; French: [al\u025bks\u0251\u0303d\u0281 \u0261ystav \u025bf\u025bl]; n\u00e9 Bonickhausen dit Eiffel; 15 December 1832 \u2013 27 December 1923) was a French civil engineer. A graduate of \u00c9cole Centrale des Arts et M\u00e9tiers, he made his name with various bridges for the French railway network, most famously the Garabit Viaduct. He is best known for the Eiffel Tower, designed by his company and built for the 1889 Universal Exposition in Paris, and his contribution to building the Statue of Liberty (Liberty Enlightening the World) in New York. After his retirement from engineering, Eiffel focused on research into meteorology and aerodynamics, making significant contributions in both fields. He was a descendant of Jean-Ren\u00e9 B\u00f6nickhausen, who had emigrated from the German town of Marmagen and settled in Paris at the beginning of the 18th century.\n\nEvidence 2: The Eiffel Tower (/ \u02c8a\u026af\u0259l / \u24d8 EYE-f\u0259l; French: Tour Eiffel [tu\u0281 \u025bf\u025bl] \u24d8) is a lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower from 1887 to 1889.\n\nEvidence 3: The Eiffel Tower (  EYE-f\u0259l; French: Tour Eiffel [tu\u0281 \u025bf\u025bl] ) is a lattice tower on the Champ de Mars in Paris, France. It is named after the engineer Gustave Eiffel, whose company designed and built the tower from 1887 to 1889. Locally nicknamed \"La dame de fer\" (French for \"Iron Lady\") for its use of wrought iron, it was constructed as the centrepiece of the 1889 World's Fair, and to crown the centennial anniversary of the French Revolution. Although initially criticised by some of France's leading artists and intellectuals for its design, it has since become a global cultural icon of France and one of the most recognisable structures in the world. The tower received 5,889,000 visitors in 2022.", "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower, https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustave_Eiffel", "verification": {"label": "supported", "confidence": 0.9979547262191772, "probabilities": [0.00029896508203819394, 0.0017463535768911242, 0.9979547262191772], "logits": [-3.3467, -1.5818, 4.7664], "evidence_scores": {"decided_by": 2, "snippets": [{"source": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gustave_Eiffel", "label": "supported", "probabilities": [0.0004943385720252991, 0.00232067983597517, 0.9971849322319031], "logits": [-3.0072, -1.4608, 4.6023], "decisive": true}, {"source": "web", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower", "label": "supported", "probabilities": [0.0003945657517760992, 0.0023620002903044224, 0.9972434043884277], "logits": [-3.2758, -1.4863, 4.5592], "decisive": true}, {"source": "wikipedia", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eiffel_Tower", "label": "supported", "probabilities": [0.00029896508203819394, 0.0017463535768911242, 0.9979547262191772], "logits": [-3.3467, -1.5818, 4.7664], "decisive": true}], "S": 0.9979547262191772, "K": 0.0, "n_sup": 3, "n_con": 0, "case": "decisive", "shared_role": false, "tau": 0.8, "m": 2}, "conformal_set": ["supported"], "coverage_guarantee": "90%", "is_escalation_candidate": false, "conformal_p_values": {"contradicted": 0.0099, "unknown": 0.0297, "supported": 0.6535}, "conformal_q_hat": 0.898471511900425, "set_size": 1, "final_decision_policy": "conformal_singleton", "trace": [{"kind": "queries", "queries": ["Eiffel Tower", "Gustave Eiffel"], "domain": "general", "temporal": false, "route": "llm"}, {"kind": "retrieval", "pass": 1, "queries": ["Eiffel Tower", "Gustave Eiffel"], "candidates": 112, "by_source": {"web": 3, "wikipedia": 109}, "avgdl": 134.1, "top": [{"text": "Alexandre Gustave Eiffel (  EYE-f\u0259l; French: [al\u025bks\u0251\u0303d\u0281 \u0261ystav \u025bf\u025bl